---
/**
 * Compare two job offers side by side: each offer through the same engine, with the verdict and
 * the table rendered at build time for the default pair and redrawn in the browser as you type.
 */
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import ComponentField from '../components/form/ComponentField.astro';
import NumberField from '../components/form/NumberField.astro';
import Segmented from '../components/form/Segmented.astro';
import SelectField from '../components/form/SelectField.astro';
import { DEFAULT_OFFERS, renderComparison } from '../lib/offers';
import { cityOptionsHtml } from '../lib/city-options';
import { STATES } from '../lib/tax/professional-tax';

const DEFAULTS = DEFAULT_OFFERS;
const initial = renderComparison(DEFAULTS);
const grouped = (n: number | null) => (n ?? 0).toLocaleString('en-IN');
const sides = DEFAULTS.map((o, i) => ({ key: i === 0 ? 'a' : 'b', o }));
---

<DocLayout
  title="Compare job offers: which one puts more in your bank"
  description="Compare two job offers side by side for FY 2026-27: monthly in-hand salary, variable pay, joining bonus after tax, income tax and PF, with a clear verdict on which pays more."
  updated="2026-10-16"
  ogImage="compare-offers"
  about={['Job offer comparison', 'In-hand salary', 'Joining bonus']}
  deva="कमाई"
>
  <p>
    A higher CTC does not always mean more money each month. Variable pay, a joining bonus, the PF
    rules and even the city change what actually reaches your bank. Enter both offers as they appear
    on the offer letters and see them side by side.
  </p>

  <form id="offers" class="not-prose" novalidate aria-label="Compare two job offers">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      {sides.map(({ key, o }) => (
        <fieldset class="min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-4 shadow-xs sm:p-5">
          <legend class="sr-only">{o.name}</legend>
          <label for={`${key}-name`} class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-3">
            {key === 'a' ? 'Offer A' : 'Offer B'}, name it
          </label>
          <input
            id={`${key}-name`}
            name={`${key}-name`}
            type="text"
            value={o.name}
            maxlength="40"
            autocomplete="off"
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xs border-0 border-b border-line bg-transparent px-0 pb-1.5 font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink focus:border-accent"
          />
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
            <NumberField
              id={`${key}-ctc`}
              label="CTC"
              value={grouped(o.ctc)}
              prefix="₹"
              width="7.5rem"
              money
            />
            <ComponentField
              id={`${key}-var`}
              label="Variable pay inside CTC"
              value={String(o.variable.value)}
              units={[
                { value: 'percent', label: '%' },
                { value: 'rupees', label: '₹' },
              ]}
              unit={o.variable.unit}
            />
            <NumberField
              id={`${key}-bonus`}
              label="Joining bonus"
              value={grouped(o.joiningBonus)}
              prefix="₹"
              width="7rem"
              hint="One-time, on top of CTC"
              money
            />
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <SelectField id={`${key}-state`} label="Work state">
                {STATES.map((s) => (
                  <option value={s.code} selected={s.code === o.stateCode}>
                    {s.name}
                  </option>
                ))}
              </SelectField>
              <SelectField id={`${key}-city`} label="City">
                <Fragment set:html={cityOptionsHtml(o.stateCode, o.city)} />
              </SelectField>
            </div>
            <details class="group rounded-md border border-line px-3 py-2">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-medium text-ink-2">
                Salary structure and rent
              </summary>
              <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 pb-1">
                <NumberField
                  id={`${key}-basic`}
                  label="Basic, % of CTC"
                  value={String(o.basicPercent)}
                  suffix="%"
                  width="3.5rem"
                  inputmode="decimal"
                />
                <Segmented
                  name={`${key}-pf`}
                  legend="PF"
                  options={[
                    { value: 'ceiling', label: 'Capped' },
                    { value: 'actual', label: 'Full Basic' },
                    { value: 'none', label: 'None' },
                  ]}
                  value={o.pfMode}
                />
                <NumberField
                  id={`${key}-rent`}
                  label="Monthly rent"
                  value={grouped(o.monthlyRent)}
                  prefix="₹"
                  width="6rem"
                  hint="Only the old regime gives relief for rent"
                  money
                />
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="panel mt-4 overflow-clip">
      <output
        id="offers-result"
        for="a-ctc b-ctc"
        class="block result-wash p-5 sm:p-6"
        aria-live="polite"
        set:html={initial}
      />
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-t border-line px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
        <button type="button" id="offers-share" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">
          <span data-share-label>Copy link to this comparison</span>
        </button>
        <p class="text-xs text-ink-3">
          The link carries both offers, so you can send it to someone or reopen it later.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>

  <h2>How to compare two offers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Start with the monthly in-hand.</strong> It is the fixed pay that lands every month,
      after income tax, PF and professional tax, and the fairest single number to compare.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Treat variable pay as a maybe.</strong> It sits inside CTC but is paid once or twice a
      year, and often at less than 100%. The table shows the year with it in full, so you can judge
      how much you are counting on it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A joining bonus is one year only.</strong> It is taxed like salary at your highest
      slab, and most offer letters ask for it back if you leave within twelve months.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>PF on your full Basic means less in hand but more saved.</strong> Some employers pay
      PF on the whole Basic rather than the ₹25,000 ceiling. Your monthly pay drops, and your PF
      balance grows by the same amount from each side.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The city matters too.</strong> Professional tax differs by state, and under the old
      regime the HRA exemption depends on your rent and whether you live in one of the eight 50%
      cities.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each offer uses the calculator's engine with Basic at the share you enter, HRA at half of Basic
    and special allowance taking the rest. For any other structure, open an offer's full breakdown
    and match each component from the letter. To see what a raise does instead, use the{' '}
    <a href="/salary-hike-calculator">salary hike calculator</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>

<script>
  import { mountOffers } from '../scripts/offers';
  mountOffers();
</script>
